# MCP Tools vs. CLI Cheat Sheet

ContextUnity ACDD exposes **dual-surface parity**: every code-graph query, linter rule, reader mode, and state-machine transition runs over the exact same Rust engine whether called by an AI agent over **MCP (`acdd serve`)** or by a developer / CI pipeline via the **CLI (`acdd ...`)**.

- **Default output**: structured Markdown on both surfaces (pass `format: "json"` in MCP or `--format json` on CLI for machine-parsed JSON).
- **Subsystem presets**: configure `preset: full | index | spec | state | minimal` in `acdd.yaml` (`spec` enables `validate`/`roadmap`/`draft` and the 4 docs/core MCP tools with zero `.acdd/state.sqlite` creation; registry-local `modules.required` mismatches emit `ACDD_WORKFLOW_SCHEMA_INVALID` with `FEATURE_REQUIRED_BY_PRESET`, while cross-layer workspace preset mismatches emit `DOMAIN_CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE`).
- **Index freshness**: MCP automatically runs incremental `delta` / `build` when files change (with a 5s inventory check cache); CLI reads `.acdd/code-map.sqlite` directly (`acdd build` / `acdd delta` updates it).
- **Worktree targeting**: MCP tools accept an optional `worktree` field on every call; CLI commands accept `-C <PATH>` (short alias for `--root <PATH>`), `ACDD_WORKTREE` / `ACDD_RUN` env fallbacks across both code/docs and state commands, plus `acdd exec [--run <id|name>] [--worker <id>] -- <program> [args...]` to run build/test/git commands directly inside the resolved worktree.

---

## 1. Code Graph & AST Navigation (9 MCP tools)

| Capability | MCP Tool | CLI Equivalent | Typical Input |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Workspace summary** | `code_map_overview` | `acdd query overview` | Optional `path` scope, `aspects: ["entrypoints", "topology"]` |
| **Symbol search** | `code_map_search` | `acdd query search <pattern>` | `"parse*"`, `"takes:Config"`, `"returns:Result"` |
| **Inspect declaration** | `code_map_inspect` | `acdd query inspect <selector>` | `"src/auth.rs:verify_token"`, `show_source: true` |
| **Direct edges** | `code_map_explain` | `acdd query explain <selector>` | `direction: "incoming" \| "outgoing" \| "both"` |
| **Blast radius / Git diff** | `code_map_impact` | `acdd query impact <selector>` | `selector` or `changes: "staged" \| "unstaged" \| "head"` |
| **Tests, removal, clones & SQL** | `code_map_query` | `acdd query tests \| remove \| run <op> \| sql` | `operation: "tests" \| "prove_removal" \| "duplicates" \| "dead_tails" \| "untested" \| "slice" \| "sql"` |
| **Diagnostics, hotspots & diff** | `code_map_analyze` | `acdd query analyze [target] [--mode ...]` | `mode: "summary" \| "hotspots" \| "boundary" \| "path" \| "entrypoints" \| "diff_impact" \| "cochange"`, `to`, `base`, `lint: true`, `include_cycles: true` |
| **Unified arch & docs lint** | `code_map_lint` | `acdd lint [target]` | `categories: ["arch", "docs", "syntax", "duplicates", "dead_tails", "cycles"]` |
| **Structural AST match** | `ast_grep_search` | `acdd ast grep <pattern>` | `'fn $NAME($$$) -> Result<$T>'`, `--lang rust` |

---

## 2. File Reader, Living Docs & Built-in Guide (4 MCP tools)

| Capability | MCP Tool | CLI Equivalent | Typical Input |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Single-shot symbol / file read** | `acdd_read` | `acdd read <path>` | `selector: "SymbolName"`, `detail: "compact" \| "full"` (`<= 9,000` B inline / `48 KiB` full), or `mode: "search" \| "delta" \| "outline"` |
| **Search Markdown sections** | `search_docs` | `acdd docs search <query>` | `doc_type: "architecture" \| "adr" \| "guide"`, `include_excerpt: true` |
| **Read doc section & links** | `get_doc` | `acdd docs get <path>` | `section: "Heading Title"`, `detail: "compact" \| "full"` |
| **Verify all doc links** | *(via `code_map_lint`)* | `acdd docs check` | Checks relative Markdown links and `#heading` anchors |
| **Interactive manual** | `acdd_guide` | `acdd guide [topic] [--mcp]` | Defaults to CLI-focused guidance across 11 topics (`query`, `init`, `adapter`, `validate`, `code`, `ast`, `docs`, `lifecycle`, `acdd`, `gates`, `subtasks`); pass `--mcp` for MCP guidance matching `acdd_guide` |

---

## 3. Workflow State Machine & Coordination (5 MCP tools + CLI)

| Capability | MCP Tool | CLI Equivalent | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Scaffold workspace** | `acdd_guide(topic="init")` | `acdd init [--force]` | Create starter `acdd.yaml`, `.acdd/workflows/default.yaml`, and `.gitignore` rules (whitelisting `.acdd/workflows/` & `.acdd/specs/`) |
| **Validate config & specs** | *(via `docs.specs` / CLI)* | `acdd validate [path]` | Fail-closed check (`ValidateReq.explicit_workflow?`) of `acdd.yaml`, workflows (`WORKFLOW_VALID`, `ACDD_WORKFLOW_SCHEMA_INVALID` + `FEATURE_REQUIRED_BY_PRESET`, or `DOMAIN_CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE`), and spec DAGs (`ACDD_SPEC_SCHEMA_INVALID`) |
| **Draft next spec file** | *(CLI only; `acdd_state` redirects)* | `acdd draft <spec> <slug>` | Create next numbered spec (`DraftReq`: `spec`, `slug`, `prefix?`, `title?`, `workflow?` → `DraftResp`: `spec_id`, `spec_path`, `spec`) |
| **Start a run** | `acdd_state(action="start")` | `acdd start <spec \| --goal> [--workflow <ref>]` | Materialize run DAG & isolated worktrees (`StateInput`: `worktree?`, `create_worktree?` → `StartReq`: `spec_path?`, `goal?`, `run_name?`, `workflow?`, `scope`, `target_base?`, `worktree`, `in_place`, `worktree_path?`) |
| **Inspect status, queue & roadmap** | `acdd_state(action="status" \| "list" \| "show" \| "next")` | `acdd status \| list \| show \| next \| roadmap [SPEC_ID] [--spec KEY]` | Active-run progress and ready cursors (`roadmap` is CLI-only: `--spec` filters by config key, positional `[SPEC_ID]` drills down; `RoadmapReq.spec?` → `RoadmapSpecEntry`) |
| **Reload context (read-only)** | `acdd_state(action="context")` | `acdd context [node] [--detail full]` | Re-render 6-tier `ClaimResp` after compaction without mutating claims |
| **Git checkpoints** | `acdd_state(action="snapshot")` | `acdd snapshot save\|restore\|list\|clear` | Save or restore scoped Git refs (`refs/acdd/snapshots/...`) |
| **Scope, sync & reopen** | `acdd_state(action="extend_scope" \| "sync" \| "reopen" \| "subtask" \| "clear")` | `acdd extend-scope \| sync [--rebind-workflow] \| reopen \| subtask \| clear` | Expand task scope, sync spec edits (`SyncReq.rebind_workflow` → `SyncResp.rebound_workflow`), reopen gates, update subtasks, or clear run |
| **Worktree command wrapper** | *(N/A)* | `acdd exec [--run <id\|name>] [--worker <id>] -- <cmd>` | Execute build/test/git commands directly inside the resolved worktree (`ACDD_WORKTREE`, `ACDD_RUN`) |
| **Headless wave runner** | `acdd_state(action="run")` | `acdd run [--jobs N]` | Automatically execute command gates and `roles.<id>.runner` CLIs |
| **Claim a gate** | `acdd_claim` | `acdd claim [node] [--detail full]` | Lock ready node (`claim_revision`) and receive 6-tier `ClaimResp` (`<= 10,000` B compact soft cap, `detail="full"` up to `32 KiB`, graceful `omitted_sections`) |
| **Run gate checks** | `acdd_verify` | `acdd verify <node>` | Execute `command:`, `checks:` (`code.seam`, `code.lint`), and scope guard |
| **Pass or reject gate** | `acdd_submit` | `acdd submit <node>` | Submit `--action pass\|reject` with proofs/findings and run `save:` policy |
| **Agent blackboard** | `acdd_blackboard` | `acdd blackboard` | Read or post `notes`, `decisions`, `blockers`, `findings`, `deferred` |
| **Domain plugin tools** | `<domain>_<name>` | `acdd tool <domain>_<name>` | Invoke custom tools registered by active `DomainProvider` plugins |
